\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Upper bounds on the second-order terms and the smoothness needed for each to be $O(r_{n}^{*})$, $r_{n}^{*}=n^{-s/(2s+1)}$, at $K_{n}\asymp n^{d/(2s+1)}$. ``Diagonal'' terms enter the estimator error linearly and must be compared with $r_{n}^{*}$ itself; ``off-diagonal'' (cross-half / $i\neq  j$) terms are mean-zero degenerate $U$-statistics. Derivations of the off-diagonal orders are in Appendix~\ref {app:proofs}. Entries are bounds, not exact orders: see Remark~\ref {rem:cancel}.}}{15}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
